    {
      "v": 1,
      "zh": "所以，我们应当离开基督道理的开端，竭力进到完全的地步，不必再立根基，就如那懊悔死行、信靠　神、",
      "en": "Therefore we must progress beyond[NOTE:1] the elementary[NOTE:2] instructions about Christ[NOTE:3] and move on[NOTE:4] to maturity, not laying this foundation again: repentance from dead works[NOTE:5] and faith in God,",
      "notes": [
        "Grk “Therefore leaving behind.” The implication is not of abandoning this elementary information, but of building on it.",
        "Or “basic.”",
        "Grk “the message of the beginning of Christ.”",
        "Grk “leaving behind…let us move on.”",
        "It is clear from the context that the phrase “dead works” are works that need to be repented from and thus are sins. The same phrase occurs in Heb 9:14 in which the author of Hebrews states that our consciences need to be purified from them. As Bruce states, they are works “that belong to the way of death and not the way of life” (F. F. Bruce, Hebrews [NICNT], 138)."
      ],
